      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-text-muted leading-relaxed">
        Trust matters more than coverage claims. ModPageSpeed runs byte-level rewrites on what
        leaves your server; it does not edit application code. These stay out of reach: excessive
        DOM size, unused JavaScript and tree-shaking, legacy-JS polyfills served to modern browsers,
        third-party script impact (analytics, tag managers, ads), Interaction to Next Paint (INP),
        forced reflows in handler code, and font-display behavior. Origin TTFB on the first request
        is also out of reach. 2.0 can mask it on repeat visits by caching HTML when the origin
        allows it, but the first hit always reaches the origin. The analyzer above labels every one
        of these in your report.
